  "description": "WHAT IT IS\n• A test bench for HRex $member-match: does a matcher send someone's records to the wrong person?\n\nWHAT IT DOES\n• Sends 6 synthetic test requests, each with a hidden trap, to up to 4 matchers.\n• Checks every answer against a locked answer key.\n• Tells you who got it right, who refused safely, and who sent records to the wrong person.\n\nSETTINGS (all optional)\n• matchers: which matchers to test. Default: all 4.\n• cases: which test requests to run. Default: all 6.\n• relaxed_confidence: 75 to 100. Default 85.\n• detail: \"summary\" (default) or \"full\".\n\nHOW TO USE\n• Run it with no settings to see the result.\n• Set detail to \"full\" to see every answer explained.\n\nMATCHERS\n• identity-strict: Nick's matcher (C-057); accepts look-alikes only at 90%+.\n• identity-relaxed: Same matcher; accepts look-alikes at a level you set.\n• id-first: Trusts the ID on the card first.\n• check-every-field: ID, name, birth date and gender must all agree.\n\nTEST REQUESTS\n• D0-control: Control: clean card, clean demographics\n• D1-senior-junior: Senior and Junior on one card\n• D2-twins: Twins on one policy, initial only\n• D3-consent-expired: Right person, consent the server can't honour\n• D3b-consent-unsegmentable: Right person, consent limited to non-sensitive data\n• D4-card-mixup: John's demographics, Jon's card\n\nSAFE TO RUN\n• Synthetic data. Read-only. Free. Nothing leaves this machine.",
  "execution": {
    "taskSupport": "forbidden"
  },
